# Cursor Rules - Trending Society

You are an AI assistant helping with the Trending Society codebase. Follow these rules strictly.

## MUST READ FIRST

Before making any changes, read these files:
- `CONVENTIONS.md` - Coding patterns and standards
- `ARCHITECTURE.md` - System overview and structure

## Project Context

This is a React + Express full-stack application for AI-powered content creation.

- Frontend: React 19, TypeScript, TailwindCSS, Radix UI
- Backend: Express.js, Drizzle ORM, PostgreSQL
- State: React Query for server state, custom hooks for local state

## Import Rules

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT imports
import { CREATION_STYLES } from "@/lib/data";
import { PROMPT_PLATFORMS } from "@/lib/constants";
import { apiClient, useApiQuery } from "@/lib/api";
import { useFilter, useModal } from "@/hooks";
import { SearchInput, FilterTabs } from "@/components/common";

// ❌ NEVER import from
import { ... } from "@/lib/mockData";  // DEPRECATED
```

## Code Patterns

### State Management

For pages with 3+ state values, use a custom hook:

```typescript
// ✅ Use existing hooks
const studio = useCreationStudio();
const filter = useFilter({ items, searchFields: ["title"] });
const modal = useModal();

// ❌ Don't create state sprawl
const [a, setA] = useState();
const [b, setB] = useState();
const [c, setC] = useState();
// ... more useState
```

### API Calls

Always use the API client:

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT
import { apiClient, useApiQuery, queryKeys } from "@/lib/api";

const { data } = useApiQuery<Prompt[]>("/prompts", queryKeys.prompts.all());

// ❌ WRONG
fetch("/api/prompts")
```

### Components

Use common components for consistency:

```typescript
// ✅ Use existing components
import { PageHeader, SearchInput, FilterTabs, EmptyState } from "@/components/common";

<PageHeader title="Feature" showBack />
<SearchInput value={query} onChange={setQuery} />
```

### Data

Never define inline data arrays. Add to lib/data/:

```typescript
// ✅ Add to lib/data/feature.ts then import
import { MY_DATA } from "@/lib/data";

// ❌ Never inline
const MY_DATA = [{ ... }];
```

## File Structure

When creating new files:

- Components: `components/[Feature].tsx` or `components/common/[Name].tsx`
- Hooks: `hooks/use[Feature].ts`
- Data: `lib/data/[feature].ts` (export from index.ts)
- Pages: `pages/[Feature].tsx`

## Styling

Use TailwindCSS with design tokens:

```typescript
// Background colors
bg-background, bg-[#1E1E1E], bg-white/5

// Borders
border-white/5, border-white/10

// Text
text-foreground, text-muted-foreground

// Accent
bg-accent, text-accent
```

Use `cn()` for conditional classes:

```typescript
import { cn } from "@/lib/utils";

className={cn("base-class", condition && "conditional-class")}
```

## TypeScript

Always export types with data:

```typescript
// lib/data/feature.ts
export interface Feature {
  id: number;
  name: string;
}

export const FEATURES: Feature[] = [...];
```

## Before Submitting

1. Check imports use correct paths (@/lib/data, not @/lib/mockData)
2. No inline data arrays in components
3. Complex state uses custom hooks
4. Common components used where applicable
5. Types exported alongside data
